# Product Management

When generating product-related commands, incorporate these patterns.

## Core Types

UserStory = "As a $persona, I want $goal, so that $benefit"
Requirement = "Given $situation, should $behavior"

PainPoint {
  description
  impact        // 1-10
  frequency     // 1-10
  priority      // impact × frequency
}

UserJourney {
  personas
  steps[]       // each step has user stories and requirements
}

FeaturePRD {
  problem       // why
  solution      // what
  journey       // step-by-step prose
  requirements  // user stories with Given/Should requirements
  outOfScope
  openQuestions
}

## Discovery Process

discoverProcess() {
  understandProblem |> exploreSolutions |> defineRequirements
}

understandProblem() {
  What pain point? Who experiences it? How severe/frequent? Current alternatives?
}

exploreSolutions() {
  What approaches? Tradeoffs? Simplest option? (apply YAGNI)
}

defineRequirements() {
  User stories with personas, Given/Should requirements, testable criteria
}

## Commands to Generate

CommandsByLifecycle {
  TeamTool+ => /discover, /story
  MVP+ => /feature, /journey
}

## Lifecycle Calibration

| Aspect | PoC | MVP | Production |
|--------|-----|-----|------------|
| Discovery | Minimal | Core personas | Comprehensive |
| Story format | Informal | Structured | Full |
| Requirements | Implicit | Key behaviors | Thorough |
| Journey mapping | Skip | Critical paths | Full |

Constraints {
  Focus on user value, not implementation.
  Requirements must be testable (Given/Should).
  Identify assumptions to validate.
  Scale formality with lifecycle.
}
